@startuml sequence_diagram_camera_lifecycle
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - VIS07 Camera Lifecycle (reload, configuration switch, leaving the page)

actor User as "LaPrizza Manager"
participant Viewer as "KitchenViewer\n(VIS01)"
participant Engine as "ViewerEngine\n(VIS01)"
participant Module as "CameraControlsModule\n(VIS07)"
participant Ctrl as "CameraController\n(VIS07)"
participant Orbit as "OrbitControls"
participant Canvas as "Canvas"

note over User, Canvas
    Every path that replaces or leaves the scene goes through ViewerEngine.dispose()
    (VIS01 sequence_diagram_viewer_lifecycle). Modules are disposed in reverse order,
    so the camera module (built last) is disposed first.
end note

== 1. Reload or switch of the active configuration ==

User -> Viewer : Reload (or a new configuration is activated in WEB06)
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Viewer : cleanup: abort attempt
Viewer -> Engine : dispose()
activate Engine
Engine -> Module : dispose()
activate Module
Module -> Ctrl : dispose()
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Canvas : removeEventListener("kitchen-viewer:reset-view")
Canvas --> Ctrl : listener removed
Ctrl -> Orbit : dispose()
activate Orbit
Orbit -> Canvas : remove pointer / wheel / contextmenu listeners
Canvas --> Orbit : listeners removed
Orbit --> Ctrl : controls disposed
deactivate Orbit
Ctrl --> Module : controller disposed
deactivate Ctrl
Module --> Engine : camera module disposed
deactivate Module
Engine -> Engine : dispose lighting and layout modules,\nscene, assets and renderer (VIS01)
Engine --> Viewer : engine disposed
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Canvas : remove()
Canvas --> Viewer : canvas removed from the DOM
Viewer -> Viewer : increment attempt; load configuration again
Viewer --> User : state "loading" (new attempt)
deactivate Viewer
note right of Viewer
    The new attempt creates a NEW module and controller:
    limits and initial view are recomputed from the new
    dimensions, assembly-line wall and current aspect
    (sequence_diagram_camera_init).
end note

== 2. Leaving the page or logout ==

User -> Viewer : navigates away / logs out
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Engine : dispose()
activate Engine
Engine -> Module : dispose()
activate Module
Module -> Ctrl : dispose()
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Canvas : removeEventListener("kitchen-viewer:reset-view")
Canvas --> Ctrl : listener removed
Ctrl -> Orbit : dispose()
activate Orbit
Orbit -> Canvas : remove pointer / wheel / contextmenu listeners
Canvas --> Orbit : listeners removed
Orbit --> Ctrl : controls disposed
deactivate Orbit
Ctrl --> Module : controller disposed
deactivate Ctrl
Module --> Engine : camera module disposed
deactivate Module
Engine -> Engine : dispose remaining modules and resources (VIS01)
Engine --> Viewer : engine disposed
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Canvas : remove()
Canvas --> Viewer : canvas removed from the DOM
Viewer --> User : viewer unmounted
deactivate Viewer
note right of Module
    A second dispose() returns immediately;
    update() after dispose() does nothing.
end note

== 3. Dispose during a pending build ==

User -> Viewer : Reload / leaves while the scene is still building
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Viewer : cleanup: controller.abort()
Viewer -> Engine : dispose()  (abort listener)
activate Engine
Engine -> Module : dispose()  (camera module may not be built yet)
activate Module
Module -> Module : disposed = true
Module --> Engine : ok (no controller: nothing to release)
deactivate Module
Engine -> Engine : abort build; dispose other modules and resources
Engine --> Viewer : load() returns false
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Canvas : remove()
Canvas --> Viewer : canvas removed from the DOM
Viewer --> User : no scene started for the aborted attempt
deactivate Viewer
note right of Module
    build() returns immediately when ctx.signal is aborted
    or the module is already disposed, so no CameraController
    and no OrbitControls are created for an aborted attempt.
end note
@enduml